  "name": "BUN/CREATININE RATIO",
  "code": "1046",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>BUN/ Creatinine ratio is used in in the differential diagnosis of ARF.<br>BUN/Cr (S) ratio &gt; 20 (fraction) indicates prerenal causes.<br>BUN/Cr (S) ratio &lt; 10 (fraction) indicates renal causes.<br>Other Non renal causes affecting BUN/Creatinine Ratio</p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 99.9989%; height: 288.496px;\" border=\"1\"><colgroup><col style=\"width: 49.8607%;\"><col style=\"width: 49.8607%;\"></colgroup>\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 33.6133px;\">\n<td>BUN/creatinine &gt;20</td>\n<td>BUN/creatinine &lt;10</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 33.6133px;\">\n<td>dehydration</td>\n<td>acute tubular necrosis</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 33.6133px;\">\n<td>hypovolemia&nbsp;</td>\n<td>liver disease</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 33.6133px;\">\n<td>shock, heart attack, severe burns</td>\n<td>malnutrition</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 33.6133px;\">\n<td>congestive heart failure</td>\n<td>pregnancy</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 53.2031px;\">\n<td>very high protein intake</td>\n<td>SIADH (syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 33.6133px;\">\n<td>gastrointestinal bleeding</td>\n<td>rhabdomyolysis</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 33.6133px;\">\n<td>advanced age</td>\n<td>corticosteroids administration or Cushing&rsquo;s syndrome</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
